<h3 style=3D"font-size:15px;margin:18px 0 6px">Risks</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Paywalled papers.</b> Pull facts like test conditions and results, u=
se NTRS copies where they exist, and don&#39;t reproduce the papers&#39; te=
xt.</li>
<li><b>The oxygen gap.</b> Forecasting above Earth-normal oxygen is an extr=
apolation. Showing exactly where the evidence stops is itself the headline =
recommendation: it tells LUCI and FM2 what to test first.</li>
<li><b>Time.</b> This is a two-person job in the time left. Post on Space A=
pps Connect tonight for an engineering or physics teammate from the Cambrid=
ge event if we need one, and one of us takes the site, story and video.</li=
>
</ul>

<h3 style=3D"font-size:15px;margin:18px 0 6px">Two other big ideas I reject=
ed</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>10,000 analyses (Trend Detective):</b> a team of AI scientists runs =
every trend test across decades of NASA Earth data, and only findings that =
convince an AI reviewer get published. It lost because most survivors would=
 be things scientists already know.</li>
<li><b>Moon base in silico:</b> evolve Moon base designs against thousands =
of simulated missions built from NASA data. It lost because it doesn&#39;t =
fit any single challenge, which costs points on relevance, and the weekend =
version would be thin.</li>
</ul>

